  "notes": "{代|か}える is a transitive ichidan verb meaning to substitute or replace with something. The intransitive pair is {代|か}わる.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pair: {代|か}わる (intransitive — to take the place of)\n- Pattern: AをBに{代|か}える (to substitute B for A)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {代|か}えている = has substituted, is using as a substitute (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AをBに{代|か}える (to substitute B for A)\n- 〜に{代|か}えて (in place of, instead of)\n- {挨拶|あいさつ}に{代|か}える (to serve as a greeting)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {代|か}える: to substitute, to use as a replacement for\n- {変|か}える: to change, to alter (modify something's state)\n- {換|か}える / {替|か}える: to exchange, to swap (interchangeable items)",
